## Zero-gap (strict)

Single approved knowledge pipeline — no parallel live crawl in chat-api. Missing capability → add (any layer/package) or refactor; exceed known architecture bar when ours falls short. Rule: `.cursor/rules/zero-gap-architecture.mdc`.

## Max capability & async collaboration (strict)

Use each stack component to **full justified capability**; services collaborate via **contracts + events** (crawl background, index async, retrieval on demand). Prod ≠ smoke limits. Rule: `.cursor/rules/max-capability-collaboration.mdc`.

## Layout reminder

```text
geostat.ops.json · apps/ · kits/geostat-kit · ops/config · tools/geostat.ps1 · docs/
```

Secrets in `ops/config` (gitignored). No internal publish/upload guides in public kit docs.

## Kit upstream

Reusable ops/tooling → **`kits/geostat-kit`** first (see `.cursor/rules/kit-upstream.mdc`). Consumer = apps + config + thin delegates.

## Kit package bar

Agnostic, manifest-driven, extensible — not a narrowed stack (see `kit-package-architecture.mdc`, `PACKAGE-PRINCIPLES.md`). **New/improved package** → discuss owner + plan first (`plan-automation-gate.mdc`, `owner-geostat-ops` skill).

## Code layout (apps/*)

Group by **logic/concern** in subfolders — not flat mixes of entities, repos, fetch, and policy in one directory. See `owner-architecture` skill and module README (e.g. `apps/ingestion-service/README.md`).
